{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774742,"nonce":"6uKdA6biqAD6iCei6ZKUl/pFMWc=","title":"fix(dogfood): make the kitchen-sink pipeline actually runnable, not just compilable","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #89 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/dogfood-pipeline-actually-runs` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-26T13:56:53Z · Merged: 2026-07-26T14:38:12Z\n\nReported symptom: the dogfood pipeline failing with\n\n```\nerror: none of the selected packages contains this feature: all\nerror: none of the selected packages contains this feature: default\n```\n\n\n`.scarab/dogfood.yaml` is a **direct child** of `.scarab/`, and trigger discovery is *\"every `.scarab/*.{yaml,yml}` at the commit, minus `.scarab/lib/**`\"*. So it has been launching on every push to main and every PR — not merely being compile-checked by `dogfood_sample_compiles`. It was authored as a teaching sample, so most of its steps could never pass.\n\n\n| Step | Problem |\n|------|---------|\n| `test` | fanned `cargo test --features ${{ matrix.features }}` over `[default, all]` — **no crate in this workspace declares `[features]` at all** |\n| `lint` | `cargo fmt --check` over everything; the workspace is not rustfmt-clean (61 diff hunks), and repo-wide `cargo fmt` is not an option here (~90 files of churn) |\n| `build` | named a root `Dockerfile` that does not exist, **and** `placement_profiles: [build-nodes]`, which is a hard failure when unregistered (`unknown placement_profile ... not in the registry`) |\n| `deploy` | ran `ghcr.io/acme/deployer:1.4.2`, a placeholder image |\n| `lint` + `test` | lacked the `CARGO_TARGET_DIR` escape `.scarab/ci.yaml` documents: the ADR-0039 baseline drops `CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE` and `/workspace` belongs to the clone uid 65532, so a run-as-root cargo cannot write there |\n\nYou would have hit these one at a time, each behind an expensive cargo compile.\n\n\nEvery step is now real, keeping the full DSL surface that makes it a useful dogfood target:\n\n- **`test`** — matrix over `crate × mode` (still 2×2 minus one exclude = 3 legs) running real cargo invocations. The service demo is now load-bearing rather than decorative: the step proves **both** shapes are reachable via bash `/dev/tcp` (the Shared service by DNS name, the sidecar on localhost), needing no client installed.\n- **`lint`** — scoped to `scarab-identity` + `scarab-pipeline`, the two crates that *are* rustfmt-clean.\n- **`build`** — points at `docker/clone`, a genuinely self-contained context with no cargo build in it, so the BuildKit leg stays fast. Sized for a single-node colima. `placement_profiles` left off with a comment, rather than faking a profile.\n- **`deploy`** — alpine, asserting the cross-step `${{ outputs.version.tag }}` actually resolved instead of just echoing it.\n- **`version`** — adds the `safe.directory` guard, since it runs as a different uid than the clone.\n\n\nHost-verifiable parts all pass: `cargo fmt --check` + `clippy` exit 0, all three matrix legs exit 0, `docker build docker/clone` exit 0. Full workspace suite: **679 passed, 22 skipped**.\n\nThe in-cluster legs (services, results capture, invoke inlining) still need a real dispatch to prove — that is the next step on this branch.\n\n\nA `build:` naming an absent context or Dockerfile compiles fine and only fails **in-cluster, after** the expensive lint/test legs it depends on have already run. `dogfood_sample_compiles` now asserts those paths exist in the repo. Confirmed it bites by restoring `context: .`:\n\n```\nstep `build` names dockerfile `Dockerfile`, absent from context `.`\n```\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}